ildren":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The NDT Industry: Growth & Opportunity"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The nondestructive testing industry is experiencing strong growth driven by aging infrastructure, increasing regulatory requirements, technological advancement, and expanding global operations. The global NDT market exceeds $10 billion annually and grows 5-7% yearly. This growth creates excellent career opportunities for skilled professionals at all levels."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Industries requiring NDT services include oil & gas (largest market), aerospace, power generation, manufacturing, automotive, pharmaceuticals, construction, and infrastructure. Each industry offers distinct career paths, compensation levels, and advancement opportunities. Some professionals specialize in specific industries or methods; others develop broad expertise across multiple sectors."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Main Content"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-12","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/guides/ndt-career-path","className":"group","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"h-full p-8 bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-lg hover:border-blue-600 hover:shadow-lg transition","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"w-12 h-12 bg-blue-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-2xl","children":"📚"}]}]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 group-hover:text-blue-600","children":"Complete NDT Career Path Guide"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 mb-4","children":"From entry-level technician to Level III certification. Learn about education requirements, certification roadmap, skill development at each level, and advancement strategies to senior positions."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-blue-600 font-semibold group-hover:underline","children":"Read the guide →"}]]}]}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/guides/ndt-salary-guide","className":"group","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"h-full p-8 bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-lg hover:border-green-600 hover:shadow-lg transition","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"w-12 h-12 bg-green-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"text-2xl","children":"💰"}]}]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 group-hover:text-green-600","children":"NDT Salary Guide by Level & Method"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 mb-4","children":"Comprehensive salary data by certification level, inspection method, region, and industry. Understand how experience, specialization, and location impact earning potential."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-green-600 font-semibold group-hover:underline","children":"View salary data →"}]]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Professional Development Opportunities"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"Training and Education"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":["Formal training programs prepare you for NDT certification. Discover ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://atlantisndt.com/training","rel":"noopener","className":"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-semibold","children":"comprehensive training programs"}]," that build the knowledge and skills required for each certification level. Most organizations offer classroom instruction combined with hands-on practical experience."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"Industry Standards and Best Practices"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":"Understanding the standards that govern NDT practice is essential for professional competence. Standards like ASTM International, API Recommended Practice, and ASME Section VIII define acceptable practice and provide technical guidance for specific applications. Staying current with standard updates ensures your knowledge remains relevant."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"Certifications and Qualifications"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":"ASNT certification is the primary professional credential in the NDT industry. The certification hierarchy—Level I, Level II, and Level III—reflects increasing expertise and responsibility. Specialized certifications in specific techniques (ultrasonic testing, radiography, magnetic particle testing, penetrant testing, eddy current testing) demonstrate expertise in particular methods."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"Continuing Professional Development"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":"Professional growth continues throughout your career. Industry conferences, technical seminars, manufacturer training programs, and peer learning all contribute to staying current with evolving NDT technology and best practices. Many organizations require continuing education for certification maintenance."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"Specialization Opportunities"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":"Consider specializing in high-demand areas like phased array ultrasonic testing, digital twin technology, or specific industries like aerospace NADCAP or oil & gas RBI programs. Specialized expertise commands higher compensation and creates competitive advantages."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white p-8 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg my-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"NDT Career Progression Overview"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold","children":"1"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900","children":"Level I Technician (Entry Level)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700","children":"Perform NDT inspections under supervision. Require 30 hours classroom training and 200 hours on-the-job training. Entry point for most NDT careers. Typical salary: $45-55K annually."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold","children":"2"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900","children":"Level II Technician (Intermediate)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700","children":"Conduct and interpret NDT inspections. Require 2 years experience (can be shortened with formal education). Supervise Level I technicians and carry greater responsibility. Typical salary: $60-85K annually."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold","children":"3"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900","children":"Level III Technician (Expert)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700","children":"Develop procedures, train technicians, and make final interpretation decisions. Require 5 years experience with 2 years at Level II. Highest certification in NDT. Typical salary: $90-150K+ annually."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-center h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold","children":"4"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-gray-900","children":"Engineer / Management Positions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700","children":"Many Level III technicians advance to engineering or management roles in NDT companies, working as quality managers, NDT supervisors, or technical specialists. Typical salary: $110-180K+ annually for senior positions."}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-16 p-8 bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-600 rounded-lg","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4","children":"Ready to Advance Your NDT Career?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-6","children":["Explore comprehensive training programs designed to prepare you for certification and career advancement. ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://atlantisndt.com/training","rel":"noopener","className":"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-semibold","children":"Atlantis NDT training programs"}]," combine classroom instruction with hands-on practical experience to ensure your success."]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://atlantisndt.com/training","rel":"noopener","className":"inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition","children":"Explore Training Programs"}]]}]]}]]}]],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","guides","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L4",null,{}],"templateStyles":